WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.858
Walk, bus, car, walk. Four
words, and no meaning at all.

2
00:00:09.078 --> 00:00:14.326
Organise them, count them, and they tell
you something. Data in, information out.

3
00:00:14.826 --> 00:00:21.095
A database is an organised collection of
data. It can live on paper, or on a computer.

4
00:00:21.315 --> 00:00:24.891
On paper it is a box of
cards, or a register of names.

5
00:00:25.111 --> 00:00:28.501
On a computer it is the
same data, stored digitally.

6
00:00:28.721 --> 00:00:34.991
Digital is fast to search and to
sort, easy to share, and very small.

7
00:00:35.211 --> 00:00:40.273
Paper needs no power and no login,
and cannot be reached from far away.

8
00:00:40.493 --> 00:00:44.069
Digital is not better at
everything. Each has its place.

9
00:00:44.569 --> 00:00:48.609
A form asks everyone the same
question, with the same choices.

10
00:00:48.829 --> 00:00:52.312
How do you get to school?
Walk, bike, car, or bus.

11
00:00:52.532 --> 00:00:58.940
Amal walks. Sami takes the bus. Zara
comes by car. Omar rides his bike.

12
00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:03.665
Eight children answer, and every
answer is written down the same way.

13
00:01:03.885 --> 00:01:09.365
Everyone got the same question, so the
answers can be counted. Nothing is missed.

14
00:01:09.585 --> 00:01:13.068
But Hana comes by scooter,
and scooter is not a choice.

15
00:01:13.288 --> 00:01:18.304
A form cannot ask why, and a bad
question gives wrong data from everyone.

16
00:01:18.804 --> 00:01:23.819
Data is the raw facts:
21, walk, cat, size 2.

17
00:01:24.039 --> 00:01:27.151
On its own, a fact like
that means nothing at all.

18
00:01:27.371 --> 00:01:31.782
Here are the eight answers again,
exactly as the children gave them.

19
00:01:32.002 --> 00:01:37.668
Walk, bus, car, bike, walk, bus, walk,
car. Which way do most children come?

20
00:01:37.888 --> 00:01:41.743
You cannot tell yet. A list of
words is data, and nothing more.

21
00:01:42.243 --> 00:01:45.818
Now organise it. Put every answer
in a table, and count them.

22
00:01:46.038 --> 00:01:51.518
Walk three. Bus two. Car two. Bike
one. That is all eight children.

23
00:01:51.738 --> 00:01:55.221
Now look at the counts. Most
children walk to school.

24
00:01:55.441 --> 00:02:00.643
Only one child cycles. That is
information: what the data means.

25
00:02:00.863 --> 00:02:05.832
Information is what you act on: a
safe crossing, and one bike rack.

26
00:02:06.332 --> 00:02:11.301
21, 19, 24, 22, 30. Five
numbers, and no meaning at all.

27
00:02:11.521 --> 00:02:16.908
That is raw data: facts as they were
collected, before anybody used them.

28
00:02:17.128 --> 00:02:22.933
Now say they are the temperatures in a
classroom, at nine o'clock, on five days.

29
00:02:23.153 --> 00:02:28.168
The last one was the day the heating
stuck on. Now the numbers mean something.

30
00:02:28.388 --> 00:02:31.732
Information is raw data that
has been given a meaning.

31
00:02:32.232 --> 00:02:36.365
A database is organised data,
on paper or on a computer.

32
00:02:36.585 --> 00:02:40.858
A form asks everyone the same
question, and it cannot ask why.

33
00:02:41.078 --> 00:02:46.139
Data is the raw facts. Information
is what those facts mean.
